  "question": {
    "text": "A fair coin is tossed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;times such that the probability of getting at least one head is at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When a coin is tossed, then probability of head,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mtext>Head</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mtext>Tail</mtext></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;(All tail)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
